From 441cf49e3535b5ef9e916fca3f0cb97e006021e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alberto Gallegos <alberto.gallegos.muro@intel.com>
Date: Tue, 21 Jul 2026 17:56:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add XPU support to FBGEMM TBE training frontend and tests

Extend the shared TBE frontend with ComputeDevice.XPU and accelerator-aware Split and Dense initialization so normal codegen modules allocate DEVICE state directly on XPU. Reject unsupported XPU placements and bounds checking explicitly.

Exercise the production constructors in the forward, dense backward, and rowwise Adagrad tests without private-state shims or collection-time monkey-patching. Keep unsupported XPU variants conditionally skipped without reducing CUDA or CPU coverage.

Signed-off-by: Alberto Gallegos <alberto.gallegos.muro@intel.com>
